The **Context Switcher** is a feature that allows users to easily switch between the public view and the management view of an engagement page. This feature is designed to enhance user experience by providing a seamless way to navigate between different contexts of the engagement.

Please note that the Context Switcher is only available to logged-in users. If you do not see your name in the top right corner of the page, use the login link in the footer to log in, which will allow you to access the Management pages.

Once you are logged in, you will see your name in the top right corner of the page. Clicking on your name will open a dropdown menu with a few options. One of these options is the "View Admin Page" or "View Public Page" depending on your current context.

[!The button to open the user dropdown menu, which contains the context switcher option](/assets/UserGuideImages/Images/context-switcher/context-switcher-dropdown.png){: .light .shadow .rounded-10}

[!The context switcher opened on the public landing page, showing the option to switch to management view](/assets/UserGuideImages/Images/context-switcher/context-switcher-public.png){: .light .shadow .rounded-10}

[!The context switcher opened on the management landing page, showing the option to switch to public view](/assets/UserGuideImages/Images/context-switcher/context-switcher-management.png){: .light .shadow .rounded-10}

When you click on the context switcher option, you will be taken to the corresponding view in the public or management context. The system will attempt to take you to the same page you are currently on, but if that page does not exist in the other context, you will be taken to the landing page of that context instead. For example, if you are authoring an engagement in the management view and switch to the public view, you will be taken to the public page for that engagement, and vice versa. If you are on a page with no public equivalent (such as the user management page), you will be taken to the landing page of the public view.

The label text for the context switcher option may change depending on the page you are on. For example, on a public engagment page, the option will say "Edit Engagement" instead. Look for the ID badge icon or the anonymous user icon next to the option to identify it as the context switcher.

[!The context switcher option on a public engagement page, labeled "Edit Engagement"](/assets/UserGuideImages/Images/context-switcher/context-switcher-public-engagement.png){: .light .shadow .rounded-10}
